<h2>Selecting and opening</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Click to select. <kbd>Shift</kbd>-click selects a range, and <kbd>⌘</kbd>-click adds or removes one item. <b>Edit → Select All</b> <kbd>⌘A</kbd> selects everything.</li>
  <li>Double-click a file, or press <kbd>Return</kbd>, to open it in its application. When no application is saved for that kind of file, Workspace asks which one to use.</li>
  <li><b>File → Open With…</b> lists the applications with their icons; those that open this kind of file come first. Check <b>Always open … files with this application</b> to remember the choice. <b>Other…</b> finds an application that isn't listed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Renaming and new folders</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Select an item and press <kbd>Return</kbd>, or click its name a second time, to edit the name in place. <kbd>Return</kbd> keeps the new name; <kbd>Esc</kbd> keeps the old one.</li>
  <li><b>File → New Folder</b> makes a folder called New Folder and lets you name it at once.</li>
</ul>
